# Secrets. This repository is published to GitHub Pages from `main`, so anything
# committed here is served publicly. `.env` holds the GOOGLE_API_KEY the render
# scripts read (they walk up from the experiment folder to find it) and must
# never be staged — a single `git add -A` would otherwise publish it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

